Here are two polished options. **Option 1** enhances the clarity and eloquence while maintaining standard, formal patent language. **Option 2** offers a streamlined, professional technical writing style.

### Option 1: Refined Patent/Technical Style (Recommended)
> The present invention relates to a method for machining and deburring gear teeth on workpieces (6) using a system that includes two workpiece spindles (3, 3′), a hobbing tool (12), and a deburring device (10). The workpieces (6) are automatically clamped into the workpiece spindles (3, 3′), gear-cut with the hobbing tool (12), and subsequently deburred according to the following process steps:
> 
> **a.** Receiving an unmachined workpiece (6) at a first loading position (19) via a first workpiece spindle (3) and transporting the workpiece (6) to the hobbing tool (12);  
> **b.** Executing a milling cut;  
> **c.** Depositing the workpiece (6) at the first loading position (19) and receiving a subsequent unmachined workpiece (6);  
> **d.** Transporting the milled workpiece (6) to a second loading position (19′);  
> **e.** Receiving the workpiece (6) at the second loading position (19′) via the second workpiece spindle (3′) and transporting it to the deburring device (10);  
> **f.** Deburring the workpiece (6);  
> 
> wherein an intermediate storage unit (14) for at least one workpiece (6) is provided between the first loading position (19) and the second loading position (19′), from which the workpiece (6) is moved into the second loading position (19′), and wherein steps **e.** and **f.** are carried out concurrently within the same time interval as step **b.**

---

### Option 2: Streamlined & Modern Technical Style
> The invention specifies a method for manufacturing and deburring workpieces (6) with gear toothings. Utilizing a setup comprising two workpiece spindles (3, 3′), a hobbing tool (12), and a deburring device (10), the workpieces (6) are automatically clamped in the spindles (3, 3′), gear-cut by the hobbing tool (12), and then deburred. The process comprises the following steps:
> 
> **a.** A first workpiece spindle (3) picks up an unmachined workpiece (6) at a first loading position (19) and moves it to the hobbing tool (12);  
> **b.** A milling cut is performed;  
> **c.** The workpiece (6) is deposited back at the first loading position (19), and a new unmachined workpiece (6) is received;  
> **d.** The milled workpiece (6) is transferred to the second loading position (19′);  
> **e.** The second workpiece spindle (3′) picks up the workpiece (6) at the second loading position (19′) and transfers it to the deburring device (10);  
> **f.** The workpiece (6) is deburred;  
> 
> An intermediate storage (14) capable of holding at least one workpiece (6) is positioned between the first loading position (19) and the second loading position (19′), from which the workpiece (6) is transferred to the second loading position (19′). Steps **e.** and **f.** are performed simultaneously within the same time frame as step **b.**

---

### Key Improvements Made:
*   **Vocabulary:** Replaced awkward phrasings like *"toothed with"* with *"gear-cut"* and *"placing down"* with *"depositing."*
*   **Flow:** Reorganized repetitive *"comprising"* and *"wherein"* clauses to make the preamble concise and easier to read.
*   **Precision:** Replaced *"in the same time interval in which... also takes place"* with the more concise *"concurrently within the same time interval"* / *"simultaneously."*
*   **Consistency:** Standardized formatting for numbering and references while preserving every original component tag and method step.
